1. Add a collapse all button in the Devices tab, to the right of the 'Deviations first' checkbox, that collapses all 3 of the packages, settings and tactical drop down tabs.
2. For the packages, settings, and tactical tabs, add an 'Apply Control Mode' button, which makes a searchable dropdown menu of all the available controls appear, as well as checkboxes to the right of each row in the table. A control can then be selected via the dropdown menu, and checking the box next to a row will add that control to the control refs of that item. The intent of this is to make it easy to assign a control to a large number of items quickly, rather than having to go through the drop down menus each time. Unchecking the boxes next to the rows will remove that control. The state of those check boxes should always reflect whether that control is applied to that row. E.g. if I set a control ref via the drop down menu, and then click the apply control mode button and select that same control, the check box to the right of that column should already be checked. If the apply control mode button is checked again, the mode should be exited and the boxes and the control select drop down menu should disappear (but the changes made obviously should stay).